## Method and Terminology Attribution

The following are original contributions first published in this repository by Akbaş:

- The Damped Resonance Alignment method and the Pusula runtime-construction technique — Phase III/IV, first published June 2026 (v1.2), with AkbasCore 1.3 DRA as the final artefact of that line.
- The magnitude-decoupled synthetic concept-injection formulation and its associated mechanisms and terminology — Phase V, first published September 2026 (v2.1).

These are documented with full mathematical specification, a public timestamped commit history, a set of permanent Zenodo DOIs (listed below), a published pre-print, and a parallel public test-log record on r/TinyLlama_TITAN and r/TinyLlama_AGI. Together these constitute the canonical reference for this method and terminology.

> **A note on scope**, stated here because it bears on what is being claimed: the Phase IV line and the Phase V line share a damping envelope and a vocabulary, but they do not share a governing equation, a model, a device, or a direction-construction method. The Mathematical Framework section of the README describes the Phase IV engine (AkbasCore 1.3 DRA). The Phase V formulation is given separately and is the one that applies to the current synthetic-injection engine. Citations should name which line they refer to.

### Suggested citation

```
Akbaş. AkbasCore: Damped Resonance Alignment — A Sub-Threshold
Inference-Layer Steering Framework for Transformer Models.
GitHub repository, v2.1, September 2026.
https://github.com/ceceli33/titan-cognitive-core

Akbaş. Damped Resonance Alignment: Closed-Loop Layerwise Activation
Steering and the Boundary Conditions of Concept Injection.
Pre-print, September 2026.
```

